    {
      "id": "s002",
      "title": "## Scene 2 \u2014 The bill I couldn't see (0:20\u20131:00)",
      "text": "I'm Ren. At twenty-five, I leased a shiny car because I wanted people to think I was doing well. By twenty-eight, I'd handed back the keys, bought a used one and survived a Christmas that left me with eighty-five dollars in my bank account. That January, I audited my bills and cut monthly payments from seven hundred and fifty dollars to four hundred and forty-five. I'm still driving that used car, eight years later. But I missed one expense. It disappeared before my paycheck arrived: the health-insurance premium. I'd never questioned it.",
